{"type":"text","timestamp":1788509539315,"sessionID":"ses_f949057d0ffeQN24RvdTqDk317","part":{"id":"prt_06b79a7a7001vS7lfB9Khu4ESv","messageID":"msg_06b799b6f001edM0WZoXrKYq4R","sessionID":"ses_f949057d0ffeQN24RvdTqDk317","type":"text","text":"Done. I implemented `rx.App(enable_state=False)` (mirroring upstream Reflex PR #5583, which this commit precedes):\n\n**`reflex/app.py`**\n- New `enable_state: bool = True` field on `App` (reflex/app.py:404)\n- `__post_init__` now calls `self._enable_state()` only when `enable_state` is true, so a disabled app skips all state setup — no `State`, no state manager, no Socket.IO server, no event namespace (reflex/app.py:486)\n- `_compile_page` no longer analyzes pages for state usage (`on_load`, stateful event triggers, state vars) or auto-enables state; state-related processing removed from the backend-only compile path and `ExecutorSafeFunctions.STATE` (reflex/app.py:851, 1149, 1347)\n- `_enable_state()` remains available for explicit opt-in after the fact (reflex/app.py:501)\n\n**`reflex/compiler/compiler.py`**\n- `compile_unevaluated_page` drops the `state` param and the enable-state detection, returning just the `Component` (reflex/compiler/compiler.py:778)\n- `compile_page`/`_compile_page` drop the `state` param and `state_name` from the page template render, so compiled pages carry no state context\n\n**Tests updated**: `tests/units/test_app.py` (state-determination test now asserts `App(enable_state=False)` stays stateless even with stateful-looking pages, plus updated app-wrap compile expectations), `tests/benchmarks/test_compilation.py`, and two integration tests.\n\n**Verification**: 3298 unit tests + benchmarks pass, ruff clean, pyright shows only a pre-existing unrelated error. A dry-run compile of an `enable_state=False` app confirms `_state` stays `None` and compiled pages contain no state context references — preventing the `$$typeof`/`Context is undefined` runtime error.","time":{"start":1788509530023,"end":1788509539310}}}
